{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"subscript","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"r","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SlsEy11SubSequenceQzqd__cSXRd__5BoundQyd__5IndexRtzluip1RL_qd__mfp"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Collection\/SubSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl11SubSequenceQa"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RangeExpression","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/RangeExpression","preciseIdentifier":"s:SX"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Collection\/Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/RangeExpression\/Bound","preciseIdentifier":"s:SX5BoundQa"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The range expression is converted to a concrete subrange relative to this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collection. For example, using a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PartialRangeFrom","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" range expression","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with an array accesses the subrange from the start of the range","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expression until the end of the array.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let streets = [\"Adams\", \"Bryant\", \"Channing\", \"Douglas\", \"Evarts\"]","let streetsSlice = streets[2...]","print(streetsSlice)","\/\/ [\"Channing\", \"Douglas\", \"Evarts\"]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The accessed slice uses the same indices for the same elements as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"original collection uses. This example searches ","type":"text"},{"code":"streetsSlice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the strings in the slice, and then uses that index in the original","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let index = streetsSlice.firstIndex(of: \"Evarts\")    \/\/ 4","print(streets[index!])","\/\/ \"Evarts\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Always use the slice’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"startIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property instead of assuming that its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices start at a particular value. Attempting to access an element by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"using an index outside the bounds of the slice’s indices may result in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"runtime error, even if that index is valid for the original collection.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["print(streetsSlice.startIndex)","\/\/ 2","print(streetsSlice[2])","\/\/ \"Channing\"","","print(streetsSlice[0])","\/\/ error: Index out of bounds"]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(1)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0